    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0196" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg104"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President
                        Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d153-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>?] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-21">21 November 1943</date>.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d153-f2"
                        /></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Former Naval Person to President Roosevelt personal and most secret. No. 506.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>My arrival in Egypt is bound to be known as I shall pass through to see
                        Catroux and others: moreover British Parliament meets on 23rd and my absence
                        must be explained. Unless I hear from you to the contrary I shall allow it
                        to be stated on 22nd that I am in Cairo.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>This publicity will be unsupported cover for your movement which I think
                        should not be announced for a few days.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>You will be receiving a telegram about military precautions<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d153-f3"/> which are excellent.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d153-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d153-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to London; forwarded to Washington, apparently via United States military
                    channels; and forwarded further by the White House Map Room to Roosevelt in
                    North Africa.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d153-f2" n="2" xml:id="d153-f2-content">
                <p>According to Alanbrooke (<ref target="#pg74">p. 74</ref>), Churchill arrived at
                    Cairo at 2:30 p.m. by plane from Alexandria.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d153-f3" n="3" xml:id="d153-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 508 of November 21, 1943, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg105">p. 105</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
